{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_18369",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase inhibitor, is linked to Immature Ovarian Teratoma through a chain of indications involving Cisplatin. This relationship is supported by the shared use of Cisplatin in multiple contexts, including the treatment of Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor of Ovary, Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome, and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor of Ovary. These conditions are all associated with Immature Ovarian Teratoma, suggesting a potential mechanistic or pathophysiological link between the tumors and Cisplatin treatment. The evidence implies that Olaparib may influence the progression or treatment response of these ovarian tumors, possibly through a mechanism involving chemotherapy sensitivity or tumor biology. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cisplatin in the pathogenesis of immature ovarian teratomas, and the potential for Olaparib to be repurposed in this context.",
